WEBVTT

00:07.010 --> 00:08.710
It was truly a cruel thing.

00:10.310 --> 00:14.110
To me, it was a painful and unforgettable event.

00:19.250 --> 00:22.220
Living is painful.

00:25.090 --> 00:27.790
But I will not forget it...

00:27.860 --> 00:31.130
No, I should not forget it.

00:31.200 --> 00:33.860
That is why I am writing this.

00:35.040 --> 00:37.370
[Note: Tanuki are Japanese raccoons and, like kitsune, are thought
to be magical creatures that can take human form.]

00:35.040 --> 00:37.370
I dedicated this to a single tanuki...

00:42.190 --> 00:50.960
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:51.000 --> 01:00.000
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

01:00.040 --> 01:06.770
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:09.380 --> 01:15.450
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:17.620 --> 01:26.190
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:26.230 --> 01:32.830
And I'm faced with another day

01:34.040 --> 01:39.770
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:39.810 --> 01:44.110
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:44.150 --> 01:48.590
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:48.620 --> 01:53.020
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:53.060 --> 01:57.550
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:57.600 --> 02:05.440
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:10.820 --> 02:14.950
SHIBAEMON TANUKI

02:16.070 --> 02:18.130
The first time I met him...

02:18.210 --> 02:20.300
I am a tanuki.

02:20.540 --> 02:23.100
When he murmured that to me, I was puzzled.

02:23.180 --> 02:26.610
I am tanuki that took human form
and now unable to return to its original shape.

02:31.120 --> 02:33.090
Ah, so you met the tanuki?

02:34.560 --> 02:39.440
The boss picked that tanuki up
somewhere... How long has he been with us?

02:41.730 --> 02:44.730
They all call him a tanuki,
but you know, keep this between us,

02:45.280 --> 02:48.490
they say he's the illegitimate
child of a very important man.

02:49.890 --> 02:52.110
That tanuki-san is a very good kid.

02:53.250 --> 02:57.370
Upon hearing that Ogin-san was
going to help some old friends in a puppet troupe,

02:57.710 --> 03:02.250
I thought that there could be someone in the troupe who
might be the next target of Mataichi and his group...

03:02.610 --> 03:05.770
Yes, in the beginning it was nothing but curiosity.

03:06.250 --> 03:08.640
No matter how I look at it, it's still a bad joke,

03:08.880 --> 03:11.110
saying that there's a tanuki here in the Shibaemon troupe.

03:11.190 --> 03:15.610
I would expect such knowledge from one
attempting to publish a book of a Hundred Stories.

03:16.190 --> 03:22.130
Note: Kappa - A well-known freshwater youkai characterized
by a dish on its head and love for cucumbers.
Bakaneko - A shape shifting cat.

03:16.190 --> 03:22.130
After all, normal people know of kappa
and bakeneko, but not of the Shibaemon tanuki.

03:22.970 --> 03:24.690
You praise me too much.

03:24.770 --> 03:31.630
It's my name too, you know. Back when I was
a kid, people used to tease me by calling me that.

03:32.010 --> 03:35.000
The troupe was called the Shibaemon Troupe.

03:35.080 --> 03:37.490
It was the name of this kindly old boss.

03:38.450 --> 03:42.850
He had the same name as the legendary
Shibaemon Tanuki, a tanuki that loved plays.

03:43.210 --> 03:47.040
It is said that it was eaten by dogs when
it took human form and went to see a play.

03:47.120 --> 03:50.590
The interesting thing is that this troupe kept a tanuki.

03:50.890 --> 03:54.140
They said that it was a tanuki that
took human shape, just like in the legend.

03:56.430 --> 03:58.560
I am a tanuki.

04:10.800 --> 04:13.470
Truly, I am a tanuki that should not be alive.

04:14.260 --> 04:17.260
I wonder, is it wrong striving to live?

04:18.010 --> 04:22.220
No, living itself is painful.

04:22.770 --> 04:24.270
The tanuki was kept in a prison...

04:24.560 --> 04:28.230
Well, the room he was kept in was
rather too luxurious to call it a prison.

04:28.810 --> 04:32.730
Perhaps the troupe took pity on his fragile appearance.

04:34.860 --> 04:36.820
That's just terrible, though!

04:37.150 --> 04:39.860
There's no need to become suddenly enraged about it.

04:40.030 --> 04:42.110
How can I not be mad about it?

04:42.280 --> 04:44.620
You're chaining a human being!

04:44.910 --> 04:50.830
It would be too shallow for a riddle-maker
to judge this matter on appearances alone!

04:51.290 --> 04:53.500
In the end, tanuki are animals.

04:53.750 --> 04:56.500
Tying up an animal is natural.

04:56.960 --> 04:58.130
But...

05:00.210 --> 05:01.210
That voice is...

05:01.880 --> 05:03.880
That is the tanuki.

05:04.300 --> 05:06.720
He's normally docile, but...

05:13.010 --> 05:17.390
That scream last night... I'm afraid I'm ashamed.

05:18.770 --> 05:21.480
Sometimes, I can't remember what I did the night before.

05:21.650 --> 05:25.650
Maybe that is the only time I return to my tanuki form.

05:25.820 --> 05:27.690
Tanuki-san, let's play!

05:27.980 --> 05:30.820
You'll be scolded by Shibaemon-dono, Tei-dono.

05:30.940 --> 05:33.530
He has told you not to come near me, correct?

05:33.780 --> 05:36.450
Grandfather is rehearsing right now.

05:36.700 --> 05:37.990
So it's fine.

05:39.910 --> 05:46.120
Me? Yes, the rumors that I am the
illegitimate son of a nobleman are true.

05:46.410 --> 05:49.670
I see... You write riddles, then?

05:49.830 --> 05:54.210
And that's why you want to hear this tanuki's story, eh?

05:56.170 --> 05:59.880
He wants me to be a double?

06:01.180 --> 06:06.930
Yes... I came into this world as a double of another.

06:07.600 --> 06:11.970
The new shogun has a weak heart.

06:12.770 --> 06:15.850
The physician said that he will surely die at a young age.

06:16.480 --> 06:17.560
If that happens,

06:17.560 --> 06:24.730
you will have to become the shogun because you
were born from the same father and look exactly like him.

06:25.820 --> 06:29.110
{Note: Ue-sama is a title of respect given to the shogun.]

06:25.820 --> 06:28.030
I will have to take Ue-sama's place?

06:29.610 --> 06:34.240
I accepted the life of a double without question.

06:34.660 --> 06:36.740
Not even permitted to go play outside,

06:36.990 --> 06:41.040
I remained inside the mansion every
day and studied Ue-sama's gestures.

06:41.960 --> 06:44.500
My sole consolation during that time

06:44.620 --> 06:50.040
was the puppet shows put on by the
Shibaemon Troupe that visited us sometimes.

06:50.380 --> 06:52.050
Ue-sama has produced an heir?

06:53.630 --> 06:55.840
Th-Then what...

06:55.920 --> 06:57.760
What will happen to me?

07:05.600 --> 07:09.270
H-How dare you!

07:19.980 --> 07:24.240
Stories of tanuki that take human form and
people who are illegitimate sons of the shogun

07:24.240 --> 07:26.030
are quite common, aren't they?

07:26.360 --> 07:30.870
Tlhat's certainly true, but they only
common if you're talking about them separately.

07:30.990 --> 07:32.870
To have both at once is...!

07:33.040 --> 07:36.120
In other words, you've taken
pity on him, haven't you sensei?

07:36.370 --> 07:37.540
Me?

07:37.710 --> 07:43.580
Feeling the pain of others as you
would your own is proof of your gentleness.

07:43.710 --> 07:45.920
Well, you could call it simplicity, too.

07:46.340 --> 07:47.550
That's enough!

07:47.840 --> 07:49.010
Going home?

07:49.510 --> 07:52.220
It's quite late now; why don't you stay for the night?

07:53.260 --> 07:56.470
Dangers, such as the random murder of
passersby, seem to be popular around here lately, too.

07:56.600 --> 07:59.760
Stuff like that can't happen all the time!

08:02.270 --> 08:04.730
Why didn't I notice then?

08:05.190 --> 08:08.100
That was his own way of
warning me, which he always used...

08:08.940 --> 08:14.400
Telling me not to get too
sympathetic to that man, that tanuki.

08:16.780 --> 08:18.030
Did I get lost?

08:19.280 --> 08:21.410
I better not move for a while, I guess.

08:23.160 --> 08:24.620
No!!!

08:33.790 --> 08:34.710
No way...

08:42.300 --> 08:43.340
Of course.

08:43.590 --> 08:45.760
There's no way he could get out of those chains.

08:48.430 --> 08:50.640
Even then, I believed.

08:50.890 --> 08:55.100
I believed that there was no way that he,
the tanuki, would just kill someone at random.

08:55.770 --> 08:58.180
Oh, the tanuki last night?

08:58.560 --> 09:02.560
He raised a big fuss,
but before we knew it, he calmed down.

09:03.310 --> 09:05.230
More importantly, they're in a big hurry outside.

09:05.400 --> 09:06.770
Go help them, will you?

09:07.320 --> 09:09.770
Yeah, another victim, right?

09:09.980 --> 09:12.360
That's disturbing, to be sure.

09:12.490 --> 09:16.530
Well, I heard that it can have a
really good time at the next stop...

09:18.620 --> 09:19.570
The tanuki can, that is...

09:21.700 --> 09:25.830
Yeah, you know, I came back in a panic once.

09:26.040 --> 09:29.460
Grandfather looked really scared that time.

09:32.420 --> 09:35.790
The murderer is traveling with the troupe?

09:36.250 --> 09:39.010
Don't say nonsense like that.

09:39.090 --> 09:44.010
If that were true, you're far more likely to become the
next victim, now that you've seen the murderer twice...

09:44.090 --> 09:45.430
Is that a threat?

09:45.510 --> 09:46.930
Take it as you will.

09:48.680 --> 09:50.970
Those aren't the deeds of a human.

09:51.310 --> 09:53.600
A human couldn't possibly do that.

09:54.140 --> 09:55.350
It's not a human.

09:59.400 --> 10:03.690
Everyone had sealed their lips
and averted their eyes from the truth.

10:04.570 --> 10:06.610
So all I could do was find it myself...

10:07.070 --> 10:10.990
find the truth of that fog-shrouded night on my own.

10:11.910 --> 10:13.200
It's about time, I think...

10:13.240 --> 10:14.570
Perhaps...

10:15.200 --> 10:17.490
Hello, Mataichi-san?

10:18.410 --> 10:19.370
What?

10:19.580 --> 10:23.370
I just wanted to see this rumored tanuki for myself.

10:23.460 --> 10:28.000
You just heard something from Ogin-san
and only came here to make fun of me, right?

10:28.460 --> 10:30.920
What you want to know is this, sensei--

10:31.090 --> 10:34.460
Is that young samurai a tanuki or a human?

10:34.670 --> 10:37.220
Did he commit those murders or not?

10:38.510 --> 10:43.720
[Note: Baketanuki are shapeshifting tanuki.]

10:38.510 --> 10:43.720
You know, baketanuki cut people
in half in order to eat their entrails...

10:44.310 --> 10:48.100
Oh, but you are well aware of that, aren't you sensei?

10:48.600 --> 10:51.140
Well, it's a well-done story, though.

10:51.770 --> 10:52.940
If he's a person, that is.

10:53.350 --> 10:54.600
If he's a person?

10:55.110 --> 10:56.360
Somebody is here.

11:01.530 --> 11:02.320
Shiba--

11:12.120 --> 11:14.240
He's gone... I lost sight of him.

11:18.460 --> 11:19.410
Tei-chan?

11:21.670 --> 11:24.210
O-Samurai-sama, please wait!

11:24.250 --> 11:26.000
O-Samurai-sama!

11:37.430 --> 11:39.390
O-Samurai-sama, calm down!

12:02.740 --> 12:03.700
Gotcha!

12:03.750 --> 12:05.160
Watch yourself.

12:06.160 --> 12:07.580
Nagamimi-san?

12:10.880 --> 12:14.590
Sensei, I don't really want to say this, but...

12:15.630 --> 12:18.260
Yeah... I didn't want to hear it, either.

12:18.840 --> 12:22.720
That Shibaemon and the
troupe members knew everything.

12:23.340 --> 12:27.430
That they knew that the young samurai was
the one who was committing the serial murders.

12:27.930 --> 12:31.470
That they undid his chains and
released him knowing he was the murderer.

12:31.720 --> 12:35.560
The young man who was once the troupe's
hope for success is now nothing more than a burden.

12:35.730 --> 12:42.650
And what's more, an unnecessary "bonus" appeared,
saying that he was going to investigate this.

12:43.280 --> 12:45.820
I-I'm a bonus?

12:45.990 --> 12:50.780
They released him knowing that
you came up here today to investigate.

12:51.030 --> 12:55.280
Basically, you were meant
to be a convenient victim, sensei.

12:57.160 --> 12:58.290
He's crying?

12:59.200 --> 13:02.910
He kills innocent people,
he killed Tei-chan, and he's crying...

13:03.620 --> 13:08.580
Do you want to know his true form?

13:11.710 --> 13:14.670
Even if it were something that Shibaemon-san planned,

13:15.300 --> 13:18.550
how am I supposed to tell him that Tei-chan was killed?

13:23.720 --> 13:24.850
Tei-chan?

13:27.390 --> 13:29.640
You're dense as usual.

13:30.140 --> 13:31.230
Ogin-san?

13:31.350 --> 13:34.270
What is the specialty of this puppeteer?

13:34.690 --> 13:36.810
That's when I understood.

13:37.270 --> 13:42.900
Mataichi and his group had come
here intending to eliminate the tanuki.

13:43.320 --> 13:44.780
I see...

13:44.910 --> 13:47.530
You've investigated well.

13:49.700 --> 13:52.330
It was a long time ago...

13:52.540 --> 13:54.620
We were after a tanuki.

13:54.660 --> 14:00.620
It was an ill-tempered thing that ravaged our
leftover food, tools, anything it could get its hands on.

14:01.500 --> 14:06.210
Then we caught "it"...
It was him, running away from the mansion.

14:08.460 --> 14:10.460
Yes, I had heard about what had happened...

14:10.510 --> 14:15.220
An heir had been born to the shogun, and the
man's hopes of replacing the shogun were a lost dream.

14:15.300 --> 14:21.680
Gone too were our troupe's dreams of
becoming the favorite of the new shogun.

14:21.970 --> 14:26.190
If we didn't think that we had been
deceived by a tanuki, we couldn't feel at peace.

14:26.850 --> 14:31.560
We couldn't just let him die; he was relying on, us.

14:33.020 --> 14:36.360
But if this were to become known,
not only would my troupe have been ruined,

14:36.740 --> 14:38.360
but our very lives would have been in danger.

14:40.160 --> 14:42.700
So, we decided to keep a tanuki.

14:43.160 --> 14:44.570
A single tanuki.

14:48.950 --> 14:51.620
What do you think we should have done with him?

14:53.370 --> 14:57.040
That man who cursed the life
in him and was succumbing to anger?

14:57.540 --> 14:58.500
That's why...

14:59.040 --> 15:00.210
You and he...

15:07.630 --> 15:12.550
I merely released a tanuki into the wilderness.

15:16.390 --> 15:21.350
He who had lost his human heart, perhaps is truly a beast.

15:21.730 --> 15:23.020
I had to think of it that way.

15:33.400 --> 15:34.570
That's Tei-chan.

15:35.070 --> 15:37.110
It was just when we got here.

15:38.200 --> 15:39.740
We couldn't save her.

15:41.740 --> 15:42.740
How awful...

15:43.410 --> 15:48.410
A tanuki who kills people on a whim must be eliminated.

15:49.790 --> 15:51.080
Eliminated.

15:53.880 --> 15:55.000
Let me...

15:56.170 --> 15:57.800
Let me do it.

15:58.050 --> 15:59.050
You?

15:59.670 --> 16:00.710
You can't.

16:01.340 --> 16:04.590
He's not a person... He's a tanuki, isn't he?

16:09.850 --> 16:15.480
Yes, he must become a tanuki.

16:17.600 --> 16:21.860
It seems that the wife of the
nobleman Hachisuka is a big lover of plays.

16:22.270 --> 16:25.650
The murders have decreased
the number of customers, too.

16:25.860 --> 16:27.940
If we get summoned to perform at her palace,

16:27.990 --> 16:30.950
we'll become prosperous again, just like the old days.

16:40.040 --> 16:41.450
Let's watch from here.

16:47.000 --> 16:49.460
You'll die with your mother, right?

16:50.590 --> 16:51.800
Mother...

17:12.900 --> 17:19.360
Yeah, that samurai over there
poisoned his mother to save his own life!

17:19.900 --> 17:24.530
With our duty over, we now
have no means to support ourselves.

17:24.900 --> 17:27.110
You'll die with me, right?

17:27.410 --> 17:29.070
Yes, mother.

17:30.950 --> 17:36.580
There was poison in my
sake cup, but none in my mothers!

17:37.460 --> 17:38.660
Why?

17:38.960 --> 17:42.500
If she took my life, would hers be saved?

17:42.710 --> 17:45.290
Did the shogun tell her that?

17:48.760 --> 17:51.130
I thought that I could go with her...

18:04.390 --> 18:10.270
I-If only you hadn't been born...

18:24.620 --> 18:26.870
Tanuki-san, what's wrong?

18:27.200 --> 18:27.830
Hey...

18:32.290 --> 18:37.120
You died... no, I know I killed you!

18:37.330 --> 18:40.290
That's right. You killed me, didn't you, Tanuki-san?

18:42.710 --> 18:44.050
You sliced me in half.

18:46.010 --> 18:46.630
Tei!

18:51.140 --> 18:52.930
I killed you!

18:53.050 --> 18:55.140
I... killed you!

18:56.430 --> 18:58.020
If I hadn't killed, I would've been killed.

18:58.060 --> 19:03.600
So I killed, again and again and again!

19:04.060 --> 19:07.690
So is that why you kill... by slicing people in half?

19:12.440 --> 19:13.780
Tei!

19:13.940 --> 19:17.610
No... don't run... I won't kill you!

19:18.530 --> 19:23.370
I won't... kill you...!

19:26.660 --> 19:30.370
Show your true form, accursed tanuki!

19:31.080 --> 19:34.630
Stop it, I'm...!

19:34.670 --> 19:36.880
Didn't you say you were a tanuki?

19:40.630 --> 19:43.970
How about you show your true form, tanuki-san?

19:44.220 --> 19:46.640
I'm not a tanuki!

19:47.720 --> 19:49.930
You are a tanuki.

19:50.010 --> 19:52.890
That's why you kill people and eat their entrails!

19:55.980 --> 20:00.860
A tanuki who has sinned
must be exterminated as a tanuki!

20:03.580 --> 20:05.870
If you insist on maintaining your own
Way, then you will aggravate people.

20:05.870 --> 20:08.540
But if you stray from your ethics,
you will fall into depravity.

20:09.040 --> 20:14.120
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

20:15.170 --> 20:17.790
Mother was supposed to have killed me.

20:17.840 --> 20:20.750
But I still live.

20:21.510 --> 20:26.590
I thought that if I killed my mother,
then this time she would kill me for sure...

20:27.430 --> 20:30.260
Is that why you continued to kill?

20:30.350 --> 20:36.270
Was it wrong to live... as though I were not human?

20:36.680 --> 20:40.480
No, but you are already dead.

20:40.730 --> 20:44.520
Your body may live, but the soul...

20:44.730 --> 20:47.650
If you wanted to die, you
should have taken your own life.

20:47.820 --> 20:52.780
All the same, you didn't kill
yourself before you killed others.

20:53.240 --> 20:54.780
That is truly a sin!

20:58.240 --> 21:00.780
I-Impossibie, he really was a tanuki?

21:01.910 --> 21:02.540
Tei...

21:05.660 --> 21:07.790
Tei-chan was killed.

21:07.960 --> 21:09.460
A long time ago.

21:11.710 --> 21:13.170
It's a curse.

21:14.000 --> 21:15.050
Of a tanuki.

21:18.170 --> 21:20.380
Tei!

21:38.020 --> 21:43.360
I wonder if it was wrong for him
to live as though he were not human.

21:43.650 --> 21:44.940
That's enough.

21:48.450 --> 21:49.740
If you understand that...

21:49.950 --> 21:51.570
Yeah.

21:52.240 --> 21:57.040
I will not forget... the tanuki I killed.

21:57.830 --> 22:02.540
For now, I will record these
still-bitter and painful emotions...

22:03.250 --> 22:05.250
I am a tanuki.

22:06.380 --> 22:09.000
and dedicate them to a single tanuki...

22:09.090 --> 22:11.880
The deed is done.

22:14.450 --> 22:20.540
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:21.890 --> 22:27.980
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:28.960 --> 22:34.730
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:34.770 --> 22:41.400
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:42.770 --> 22:48.710
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:48.750 --> 22:55.410
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:56.250 --> 23:05.720
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:07.030 --> 23:10.230
Draw near

23:10.500 --> 23:17.500
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:17.540 --> 23:23.480
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:25.650 --> 23:30.920
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:30.960 --> 23:39.590
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:49.510 --> 23:54.840
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:55.220 --> 23:58.600
Head west from Kyoto,
and you'll find a land of transience.

23:59.010 --> 24:01.180
Genba Sasayama lost his wife.

24:01.600 --> 24:05.140
Emotions without an outlet
end up residing in a woman's corpse.

24:05.600 --> 24:09.650
Next time on Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 stories,

24:10.140 --> 24:11.470
Katabiragatsuji

24:12.440 --> 24:14.610
The deed has been done.
